Since today TuxMobil lists more than 5,000 Linux laptop installation
guides ( http://tuxmobil.org/mylaptops.html ). Members of the Linux
community from all over the world provide help documents in different
languages. These documents are helpful for beginners as well as for
experts. From guides for old laptops with 286 CPU to instructions for
current machines with Intel Core Duo and AMD64 processors, there is help
available. Also tips and tricks for BSD and other UNIX derivatives are
provided. TuxMobil has become the largest database about Linux and laptops
now.

